# Configuration Standards

## Next.js Config

- File must be `next.config.ts` (TypeScript, ESM), not `.js` or `.mjs`
- Use `import type { NextConfig }` and `export default`

## Tailwind Config

- All theme colors must reference CSS variables, never hardcoded hex:

```typescript
colors: {
  accent: {
    DEFAULT: "var(--color-accent)",
    dark: "var(--color-accent-dark)",
    light: "var(--color-accent-light)",
  },
}
```

- Content paths: only `./src/components/**/*` and `./src/app/**/*` (no `src/pages/`)
- Remove unused theme extensions; don't add values that components use via arbitrary values

## TypeScript Config

- `"jsx": "preserve"` (Next.js SWC handles transformation)
- Path alias: `"@/*": ["./src/*"]`

## ESLint

- Uses flat config: `eslint.config.mjs`
- Extends `eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals` natively (no `FlatCompat` wrapper)
- Ends with `eslint-config-prettier` so ESLint does not fight Prettier
- Lint script: `"lint": "eslint ."`
- Format scripts: `"format": "prettier --write ."`, `"format:check": "prettier --check ."`

## PostCSS

- Must include both `tailwindcss` and `autoprefixer` plugins

## CI/CD (GitHub Actions)

Keep **PR CI** and **Deploy** as separate workflows — do not collapse them:

- **PR / branch CI** (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`): pull requests to `main`, and pushes except `main`/`gh-pages`. Jobs: lint + Prettier `format:check` + typecheck + unit tests (`npm test` = Vitest + Python OSV-gate) + build (artifact `out`), cspell, lychee, knip, Playwright (needs the `out` artifact). Concurrency cancels in-progress runs on the same ref.
- **Gitleaks** (`.github/workflows/gitleaks.yml`): pull requests to `main` and pushes to `main`. Official `gitleaks/gitleaks-action@v3` with `fetch-depth: 0` and `GITLEAKS_VERSION` **8.30.1**. `GITHUB_TOKEN` is limited to `contents: read` and `pull-requests: write` (checkout, PR commit listing, leak comments). The job fails if secrets are detected. Config is `.gitleaks.toml` (default rules plus a documented, AND-scoped allowlist).
- **OSV-Scanner** (`.github/workflows/osv-scanner.yml`): pull requests to `main` and pushes to `main`. Official `google/osv-scanner-action/osv-scanner-action` pinned to v2.5.1 on `package-lock.json`. The job **fails on HIGH and CRITICAL** (CVSS ≥ 7.0 via `.github/scripts/osv-fail-on-high-critical.py`). Medium/low do not fail. Missing `max_severity` falls back to GitHub `database_specific.severity` when that label is HIGH or CRITICAL; findings with no score and without those labels do not fail. Gate unit tests: `tests/unit/test_osv_fail.py` (runs under `npm test`). No blanket ignore; `osv-scanner.toml` `IgnoredVulns` only with a written why. Favicon ICO packing is local in `tools/generate-favicon.mjs` (do not reintroduce `to-ico`).
- **Deploy** (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`): push to `main` only. `npm ci` → `lint` → `typecheck` → `build` → `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages` (`publish_dir: ./out`). Does **not** run `format:check`, `npm test`, Gitleaks, or OSV — those are separate workflows. Never deploy from feature branches.

Shared rules:

- Pin Node with `node-version-file: .nvmrc` (currently 22)
- Use `npm ci` in CI, not `npm install`
- Playwright serves the static export (`npx serve out` on port 4173). Tests must `npm run build` first locally
- Lychee config is `lychee.toml` (accept 403/429/999; exclude bot-blocked hosts)
- Dependabot (`.github/dependabot.yml`) groups minor/patch updates and **ignores all semver-major** bumps. Tailwind must stay on v3. Vitest 5 needs Node 22 (the runtime this repo pins).

## Tailwind version pin

- Runtime dependency is `tailwindcss@^3.4.19` with `postcss` + `autoprefixer`
- Tailwind v4 is a breaking PostCSS plugin change. Do not bump the major in this repo without a dedicated migration
